abstract:
We present searches for the leptonic decays $B^{+} 	o \ell^{+} 
u$ and the lepton flavor violating decays $B^{0} 	o \ell^{\pm} 	au^{\mp}$, where $\ell = e, \mu$, with data collected by the BaBar detector at the PEP-II asymmetric-energy $e^{+}e^{-}$ collider at SLAC. Using 378 million $B ar{B}$ pairs, we find no evidence for signal in any of the decay modes and set the following 90% confidence level upper limits: $\mathcal{B}(B^{+} 	o e^{+} 
u) < 5.2 	imes 10^{-6}$, $\mathcal{B}(B^{+} 	o \mu^{+} 
u) < 5.6 	imes 10^{-6}$, $\mathcal{B}(B^{0} 	o e^{+} 	au^{-}) < 2.8 	imes 10^{-5}$ and $\mathcal{B}(B^{0} 	o \mu^{+} 	au^{-}) < 2.2 	imes 10^{-5}$.
